      "continuation": false,
      "heading_level": null,
      "md_text": "Bit 1, DSKBLK, indicates “disk block finished.” It is used to indicate that the specified disk DMA task that you have requested has been completed. This bit generates a level 1 interrupt.",
      "bbox": [
        358,
        229,
        2151,
        327
      ],
      "segment_id": "page_0137_seg_001"
    },
    {
      "type": "prose",
      "continuation": false,
      "heading_level": null,
      "md_text": "More information about disk data transfer and interrupts may be found in Chapter 8, “Interface Hardware.”",
      "bbox": [
        358,
        389,
        2154,
        490
      ],
      "segment_id": "page_0137_seg_002"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "continuation": false,
      "heading_level": 2,
      "md_text": "Serial Port Interrupts",
      "bbox": [
        359,
        610,
        783,
        655
      ],
      "segment_id": "page_0137_seg_003"
    },
    {
      "type": "prose",
      "continuation": false,
      "heading_level": null,
      "md_text": "The following serial interrupts are associated with the specified bits of the interrupt registers.",
      "bbox": [
        358,
        744,
        2045,
        789
      ],
      "segment_id": "page_0137_seg_004"
    },
    {
      "type": "prose",
      "continuation": false,
      "heading_level": null,
      "md_text": "Bit 11, RBF (for receive buffer full), specifies that the input buffer of the UART has data that is ready to read. This bit generates a level 5 interrupt.",
      "bbox": [
        360,
        852,
        2153,
        951
      ],
      "segment_id": "page_0137_seg_005"
    },
    {
      "type": "prose",
      "continuation": false,
      "heading_level": null,
      "md_text": "Bit 0, TBE (for “transmit buffer empty”), specifies that the output buffer of the UART needs more data and data can now be written into this buffer. This bit generates a level 1 interrupt.",
      "bbox": [
        361,
        1013,
        2155,
        1111
      ],
      "segment_id": "page_0137_seg_006"
    },
